COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[269,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you explain that those who are invoked besides Allah are unable to do harm or good to themselves, let alone others.\nSeek refuge with Allah from arrogance and conceit.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness for circulating any message or story that contains sin, for you will bear the burden of it, and the burden of sin of every person who has seen and acted upon it till the Day of Resurrection.\nguid\nYou cannot thank Allah enough for all of His blessings, but be a thankful servant; that is, those who give thanks often.\nBeware of bearing the burden of sins of others on the Day of Resurrection, by leading someone to commit a sin, or reminding him of it.\nEvil plotting does not encompass except its own people.\nrefl\nوَأَلۡقَىٰ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ رَوَٰسِيَ أَن تَمِيدَ بِكُمۡ وَأَنۡهَٰرٗا وَسُبُلٗا لَّعَلَّكُمۡ تَهۡتَدُونَ ١٥\nThis verse proves the adoption of means to reach an end. Al-Qurtubi: 12/305.\nDoes reliance upon Allah contradicts the adoption of means? Explain.\nوَإِن تَعُدُّواْ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ لَا تُحۡصُوهَآۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ١٨\n(If you try to count Allah's blessings) without thanking Him (you will not be able to enumerate them), let alone give proper thanks, as His blessings to His servants, both apparent and hidden, are as many as the breaths they take and the moments that pass. This applies to all kinds of blessings, both those of which people are aware and those of which they are not. Moreover, what He wards off from them of calamities are even more than they can be counted. (Indeed, Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful), He is pleased with a little thanks from you, even though His blessings are so many. Al-Saadi: 437\nThe verse ends with (Indeed, Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful), why?\nوَإِن تَعُدُّواْ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ لَا تُحۡصُوهَآۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ١٨\nFrom the beginning of this Surah up to this verse, Allah enumerates a wide variety of His creations as a proof of His Oneness, and that is why they are followed by this verse: (Is then He Who creates equal to one who cannot create?). Moreover, they include the enumeration of His blessings upon His creation, and that is why they are followed by this verse: (And if you try to count Allah's blessings, you will not be able to enumerate them), then, He says, (Indeed, Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful) which means that He forgives your shortcoming in thanking Him for His blessings. Ibn Juzay: 1/460.\nThe verse ends with (Indeed, Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful), why?\nوَٱللَّهُ يَعۡلَمُ مَا تُسِرُّونَ وَمَا تُعۡلِنُونَ ١٩\nAllah asserts that He knows what is concealed, as well as, what is revealed. He will recompense everyone for their deeds on the Day of Resurrection. If their deeds are good, they will be rewarded, but if their deeds are evil, they will be punished. Ibn Kathir: 2/546.\nWhat is the practical benefit of knowing that Allah knows what you conceal and reveal?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ لَا يَخۡلُقُونَ شَيۡـٔٗا وَهُمۡ يُخۡلَقُونَ ٢٠ أَمۡوَٰتٌ غَيۡرُ أَحۡيَآءٖۖ وَمَا يَشۡعُرُونَ أَيَّانَ يُبۡعَثُونَ ٢١\n(They are [in fact] dead, not alive), the reason for using the term (not alive) after (dead) is that some things that can be lifeless at one point may become alive afterward, such as a sperm-drop, so the term (not alive) is mentioned to guard against this meaning. Moreover, this is as saying: They are dead and will never be alive. Al-Alusi: 14/485.\nIn describing the gods of the polytheists, the term (not alive) is used after (dead). Why?\nلِيَحۡمِلُوٓاْ أَوۡزَارَهُمۡ كَامِلَةٗ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ وَمِنۡ أَوۡزَارِ ٱلَّذِينَ يُضِلُّونَهُم بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٍۗ أَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَزِرُونَ ٢٥\nThey misguide those who do not know of their misguidance, which indicates that their evil plot does not deceive a prudent person, and only ignorant people will follow them. This is also a rebuke to them for not guiding the ignorant instead of misguiding them. This verse is quoted as evidence that a person who follows a scholar must look for and distinguish between the truthful and the falsifier since he is not exempt from responsibility due to his ignorance. Al-Alusi: 489-490.\nIn light of this verse, discuss the downsides of ignorance and following others in religious matters.\nوَأَتَىٰهُمُ ٱلۡعَذَابُ مِنۡ حَيۡثُ لَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٢٦\nMeaning: The punishment came upon them from where they thought it was a secure side. Al-Qurtubi: 12/314.\nDoes punishment often come from a secure side or an insecure one?\nwords\nرَوَاسِيَFirm mountains\nأن تَمِيدَSo it does not tremor\nأَيَّانَWhen\nلا جَرَمَCertainly\nأَسَاطِيرُStories, fables\nأَوزَارَهُمBurdens of sins\nفَخَرَّFell down"],[270,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nDo not abandon the pursuit of knowledge. Attend a lesson, a lecture, or read a book, for Allah, the Almighty, will elevate the people of knowledge in this world and the Hereafter.\nIdentify several good deeds for which Allah has admitted those who performed them into Paradise, and start doing one of them today.\nAsk Allah for a good end of life.\nguid\nAmong satan's manipulations of weak minds is making them believe that adherence to revelation is synonymous with backwardness.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, devout scholars will bear witness to the actions of the people of this world, therefore, you should follow them in this world to be aware of what Allah loves and what pleases Him.\nBeware of mocking or ridiculing preachers to Allah and reforming scholars.\nrefl\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ إِنَّ ٱلۡخِزۡيَ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ وَٱلسُّوٓءَ عَلَى ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٢٧\nThis highlights the virtue of the scholars, for they are the speakers of truth in this world, and will be the speakers of truth on the Day of Resurrection, for their words carry weight before Allah and before His creation. Al-Saadi: 439.\nWhat is the virtue of the scholars according to this verse?\nٱلَّذِينَ تَتَوَفَّىٰهُمُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ ظَالِمِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡۖ فَأَلۡقَوُاْ ٱلسَّلَمَ مَا كُنَّا نَعۡمَلُ مِن سُوٓءِۚ بَلَىٰٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلِيمُۢ بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ٢٨\nThis will occur at some stage of the Day of Resurrection; they will deny what they used to do in this world, thinking that this will benefit them. But when their physical faculties testify against them, and what they used to do becomes clear, they will admit it and confess. Hence, they will not enter hell until they admit their sins. Al-Saadi: 439.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the polytheists will deny their sins and admit them. How?\nفَٱدۡخُلُوٓاْ أَبۡوَٰبَ جَهَنَّمَ\nAll those who committed a particular deed will enter through the appropriate gate. Al-Saadi: 439.\nThere are seven gates for Hellfire; through which gate do the disbelievers enter?\nفَٱدۡخُلُوٓاْ أَبۡوَٰبَ جَهَنَّمَ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَاۖ فَلَبِئۡسَ مَثۡوَى ٱلۡمُتَكَبِّرِينَ ٢٩\nThey will enter Hellfire from the day they die with their souls, and their bodies will feel the heat and scorching wind in their graves. When the Day of Resurrection comes, their souls will be reunited with their bodies, to abide forever in the fire of Hell. Ibn Kathir: 2/548.\nAfter death, the disbeliever goes through two stages of torment. What are they?\nوَقِيلَ لِلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ مَاذَآ أَنزَلَ رَبُّكُمۡۚ قَالُواْ خَيۡرٗاۗ لِّلَّذِينَ أَحۡسَنُواْ فِي هَٰذِهِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا حَسَنَةٞۚ وَلَدَارُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ خَيۡرٞۚ وَلَنِعۡمَ دَارُ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٣٠\nThe good reward in this world is the good life, and what Allah has bestowed upon them of the enjoyment in this world with the blessing of faith. Ibn Ashur: 14/142.\nAccording to this verse, what is the good reward in this world?\nجَنَّٰتُ عَدۡنٖ يَدۡخُلُونَهَا تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُۖ لَهُمۡ فِيهَا مَا يَشَآءُونَۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يَجۡزِي ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٣١\n(They will have therein whatever they wish), man will never find everything he wants except in Paradise! So, reflect on this meaning. Al-Alusi: 14/500.\nHow should the believer think about what he misses from the pleasures and adornment of this world?\nٱلَّذِينَ تَتَوَفَّىٰهُمُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ طَيِّبِينَ\nTheir hearts are content with knowing and loving Allah, their tongues constantly remember and praise Him, and their physical faculties are constantly focused on acts of obedience and turning to Him. Al-Saadi: 439.\nHow can you make your soul good and pure in death?\nwords\nيُخزِيهِمHe will disgrace them with punishment\nتُشَاقُّونَ فِيهِمThose whom you opposed the Prophets for\nفَأَلقَوُا السَّلَمَThey will offer submission\nمَثوَىAbode\nيَنظُرُونَThey wait\nوَحَاقَThey will be surrounded"],[271,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nConvey a useful subject matter to some of your friends or brothers, following the example of the Prophets and treading their path .\nIdentify three reasons for Allah's destruction of deniers.\nGuidance can only come when Allah wills, so ask Him for guidance.\nguid\nEmphasize the Oneness of Allah in your learning, teaching and preaching.\nReflect on the state of affairs of the previous nations whenever you walk through their ruins or read about them; it will help assure the Oneness of Allah and settle it in your heart.\nBear patiently with your worship and put your trust in Allah, the Almighty, in all of your affairs, for this is the reason of success.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ بَعَثۡنَا فِي كُلِّ أُمَّةٖ رَّسُولًا أَنِ ٱعۡبُدُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱجۡتَنِبُواْ ٱلطَّٰغُوتَۖ\nAllah continued to send Messengers to the people since shirk began to spread among the children of Adam from the time of Noah (u), the first Messenger, until the time of the last Messenger, Muhammad (ﷺ), and the Message of all the Messengers is one as Allah says, (And We sent not before you any messenger except We revealed to him that, \"There is no deity except Me, so worship Me\") [21:25]. This is similar to what Allah says in this verse, so after all this, how can a polytheist justify saying, (If Allah had willed, we would not have worshipped anything other than Him)!? Al-Qasimi: 4/516.\nWhat is the benefit in knowing that all the Messengers from Noah (u) until the time of Prophet (ﷺ) came with the same Message?\nوَأَقۡسَمُواْ بِٱللَّهِ جَهۡدَ أَيۡمَٰنِهِمۡ لَا يَبۡعَثُ ٱللَّهُ مَن يَمُوتُۚ بَلَىٰ وَعۡدًا عَلَيۡهِ حَقّٗا وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٨\nWhat seems bewildering is that they revere Allah, and swear by His Name, yet they do not believe that He can resurrect the dead. Al-Qurtubi: 12/324.\nIn this verse, the oath of the deniers seems bewildering. How?\nوَلِيَعۡلَمَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ كَٰذِبِينَ ٣٩\nWhen they see that their deeds result in regret and realize that the gods on whom they called besides Allah will avail them nothing, when the decree of your Lord (namely His punishment) comes to pass, and they see what they used to worship become fuel for Hellfire, for the sun and moon will be rolled up, the stars will be scattered, and it will become clear to those who worshiped them that they were subjugated slaves of Allah who were in need of Him at all times. Al-Saadi: 440.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, how will the disbelievers know that their leaders were liars?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُواْ فِي ٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا ظُلِمُواْ لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمۡ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا حَسَنَةٗۖ وَلَأَجۡرُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ أَكۡبَرُۚ لَوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤١\nThis may have been revealed concerning those who migrated to Abyssinia; they left their homes and wealth, but Allah compensated them with something better in this world. Whoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will compensate him with something better, and this is what happened. (If only they knew), if those who stayed behind and did not migrate with them only knew what Allah had prepared for those who obeyed Him and followed His Messenger. Ibn Kathir: 2/551.\nWhoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will compensate him with something better. Discuss this in light of this verse.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُواْ فِي ٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا ظُلِمُواْ لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمۡ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا حَسَنَةٗۖ وَلَأَجۡرُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ أَكۡبَرُۚ لَوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤١\nQatadah said: Those were the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) who were persecuted by the polytheists in Makkah, and driven out of their homes until some of them migrated to Abyssinia, then Allah settled them in Madinah afterward, made it a migration destination, and provided them with help from the believers. Al-Qurtubi: 2/615.\nWhich Quranic verse you would cite to console the persecuted and oppressed in our present times?\nٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُواْ وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ ٤٢\nIn the Arabic text, (endured patiently) is in the past tense form, while (put their trust in their Lord) is in the present tense form to indicate that their endurance will soon be over due to the end of its causes, and that Allah has made a way out for them through the current migration and the anticipated one, so this is good news to them. Reliance upon Allah is a habit of theirs since they face great endeavors that are accomplished through putting their trust in Allah in all of their affairs. Moreover, with their continuous reliance upon Allah, they are assured of success. Ibn Ashur: 14/159.\n(Endured patiently) is in the past tense form while (put their trust in their Lord) is the present tense form. Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُواْ وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ ٤٢\n(And put their trust in their Lord) in all of their affairs. Some insightful scholars said: The best among people is the one who when afflicted with disaster, endures patiently, and when he is faced with difficulty, relies upon Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 12/328.\nWhat are the more prominent traits of the best among people, which are mentioned by Allah?\nwords\nالطَّاغُوتَAnything that is worshiped other than Allah\nجَهدَ أَيمَانِهِمThey swore using strongest oaths\nلَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمWe will surely settle them\nحَسَنَةًA good place"],[272,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nRead a Prophetic Hadith or more from the section on the interpretation of Quran in Sahih Al-Bukhari, and reflect on how Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) explains the Quran.\nLearn the meanings of Allah's Names: (Ever Gracious) and (Most Merciful), and supplicate Allah by them.\nRecall a great blessing that is bestowed by Allah upon you, and say, \"Allah bestowed upon me such a blessing.\" Never attribute this blessing to anyone else or to yourself.\nguid\nTurn to the people of knowledge to clarify any ambiguous issue that you may have, and avoid contriving.\nYou will not be able to understand the aims and particulars of the Quran without learning the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ).\nThe persistent on disobedience may be punished from where he does not perceive nor expect.\nrefl\nفَسۡـَٔلُوٓاْ أَهۡلَ ٱلذِّكۡرِ إِن كُنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٣\nThis implies praise for people of knowledge, as Allah instructed us to ask them so that the ignorant one may do what is required of him, and this indicates that Allah entrusted them with His revelation. Al-Saadi: 441.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of the people of knowledge. Explain.\nفَسۡـَٔلُوٓاْ أَهۡلَ ٱلذِّكۡرِ إِن كُنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٣ بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ وَٱلزُّبُرِۗ وَأَنزَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ ٱلذِّكۡرَ\nThe best people of knowledge are those who have knowledge of this Holy Quran, for they are people of knowledge in a true sense and are more deserving of this title than others. Hence, Allah says: (and We have sent down to you the Reminder), the Quran. Al-Saadi: 441.\nThe best people of knowledge are those who are closer to the Quran. Explain in light of this verse.\nأَوۡ يَأۡخُذَهُمۡ عَلَىٰ تَخَوُّفٖ فَإِنَّ رَبَّكُمۡ لَرَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٌ ٤٧\n(Or that He will seize them when they are in a state of fear), there are two possible meanings for the term (a state of fear), first: A state of decrement, which is a gradual decline in their wealth and souls until they are completely eradicated without having to destroy them all at once, and that is why Allah says, (But your Lord is indeed Ever Gracious, Most Merciful) because this type of punishment is lighter than others. Omar Bin Al-Khattab did not know the exact meaning of this term (a state of fear) until a man from the tribe of Huthail said to him: \"In our dialect, a state of fear is a state of decrement.\" Second: It is fear, whereby Allah destroys other people before them, thus they become fearful of being punished, then Allah destroys them after they feared and expected His punishment. Ibn Juzay: 1/465.\nWhat is meant by (He will seize them when they are in a state of fear)?\nأَفَأَمِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ مَكَرُواْ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ أَن يَخۡسِفَ ٱللَّهُ بِهِمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ أَوۡ يَأۡتِيَهُمُ ٱلۡعَذَابُ مِنۡ حَيۡثُ لَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٤٥ أَوۡ يَأۡخُذَهُمۡ فِي تَقَلُّبِهِمۡ فَمَا هُم بِمُعۡجِزِينَ ٤٦ أَوۡ يَأۡخُذَهُمۡ عَلَىٰ تَخَوُّفٖ فَإِنَّ رَبَّكُمۡ لَرَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٌ ٤٧\nBut Allah is the Most Gracious, Most Merciful, and He does not hasten the punishment for the sinners; rather He gives them respite, grants them well-being and bestows provision upon them, whilst they offend Him and His allies. Despite that, He opens the gates of repentance to them, calls them to give up the bad deeds that harm them, and promises in return for that the best rewards and forgiveness for what they have committed of sins. Al-Saadi: 441.\nThese verses of threat conclude with Allah's Names: Ever Gracious, Most Merciful. Why?\nيَخَافُونَ رَبَّهُم مِّن فَوۡقِهِمۡ وَيَفۡعَلُونَ مَا يُؤۡمَرُونَ۩ ٥٠\nAt the completion of reciting this verse, the reader should prostrate, and the wisdom behind it is showing that the believer is among those whom Allah praised as being similar to the angels in prostrating to Allah, the Almighty. Ibn Ashur: 14/171.\nWhat is the wisdom behind prostrating after reciting this verse?\nوَقَالَ ٱللَّهُ لَا تَتَّخِذُوٓاْ إِلَٰهَيۡنِ ٱثۡنَيۡنِۖ إِنَّمَا هُوَ إِلَٰهٞ وَٰحِدٞ\nThe command to fear, and fear Allah alone indicates that all power is with Him, thus hope should also be sought in Him alone. Ibn Ashur: 14/174.\nWhat is the benefit of commanding people to fear, and fear Allah alone?\nوَمَا بِكُم مِّن نِّعۡمَةٖ فَمِنَ ٱللَّهِۖ ثُمَّ إِذَا مَسَّكُمُ ٱلضُّرُّ فَإِلَيۡهِ تَجۡـَٔرُونَ ٥٣\nMeaning: How can you fear other than Allah while every blessing you have is from Him alone. (To Him alone you cry out for help), you humbly call out on Him to help you. Ibn Juzay: 1/466.\nHow can you infer from this verse that Oneness of Allah is a natural disposition of man?\nwords\nوَالزُّبُرِThe Scriptures\nمَكَرُوا السَّيِّئَاتِThose who have planned evil deeds\nيَتَفَيَّأُInclines\nدَاخِرُونَThe are humble to the Greatness of Allah\nوَاصِبًاPermanently"],[273,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you clarify the status of women during past and current times of ignorance, and their status in Islam.\nGlorify Allah by His Names: (All-Mighty) and (All-Wise), and know that honor and wisdom can only be attained from Him, so ask for them from their owner, the Almighty.\nAsk Allah to grant you guidance and mercy through His Book.\nguid\nWhen the believer remembers that he will be held accountable for his words and deeds before Allah, he will guard against saying or doing evil.\nTreat your daughters and sisters well, and receive them with delight.\nBeware of being among those whom satan makes their evil deeds appealing to them; where he makes evil deed appear good to them, and good deed appear evil to them while they are in heedlessness.\nrefl\nوَيَجۡعَلُونَ لِمَا لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ نَصِيبٗا مِّمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡۗ\nThey allocated to their idols -that knew nothing and could not bring any benefit or ward off any harm- a share of what Allah had provided and blessed them with. They used the provision that He had bestowed to associate others with Him and to draw closer to carved idols. Al-Saadi: 442.\nDescribe the polytheists ignorance in trying to draw closer to those whom they associated with Allah.\nتَٱللَّهِ لَتُسۡـَٔلُنَّ عَمَّا كُنتُمۡ تَفۡتَرُونَ ٥٦\nAllah swore by His Almighty Self to question them about these lies and fabrications. He will most certainly call them to account for it and give them the unrelenting punishment in Hellfire. Ibn Kathir: 2/554.\nWhat is aim behind informing that they will be questioned about their fabrications?\nوَإِذَا بُشِّرَ أَحَدُهُم بِٱلۡأُنثَىٰ ظَلَّ وَجۡهُهُۥ مُسۡوَدّٗا وَهُوَ كَظِيمٞ ٥٨ يَتَوَٰرَىٰ مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ مِن سُوٓءِ مَا بُشِّرَ بِهِۦٓۚ أَيُمۡسِكُهُۥ عَلَىٰ هُونٍ أَمۡ يَدُسُّهُۥ فِي ٱلتُّرَابِۗ أَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَحۡكُمُونَ ٥٩\nThis verse clearly censures those who become saddened when they are given the good news of a female baby, and it attributes this attitude to the disbelievers. Ibn Jarir narrated that Qatadah said about this verse: \"This was the attitude of Arab polytheists; where Allah informed you of their evil way, however, a true believer is obliged to accept what Allah has given him since Allah's decree for him is always better than his own choice. By Allah, we never know what is best; perhaps a daughter will be much better than a son for their family. Allah informed you of their evil way, so that you avoid it.\" Al-Alusi: 14/549.\nWhat should a Muslim do when his wife gives birth to a baby whose gender is contrary to what he wishes for?\nوَلَوۡ يُؤَاخِذُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلنَّاسَ بِظُلۡمِهِم مَّا تَرَكَ عَلَيۡهَا مِن دَآبَّةٖ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَخِّرُهُمۡ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗىۖ فَإِذَا جَآءَ أَجَلُهُمۡ لَا يَسۡتَٔۡخِرُونَ سَاعَةٗ وَلَا يَسۡتَقۡدِمُونَ ٦١\n(If Allah were to take people to task for their wrongdoing), no more and no less (He would not have left upon it [the earth] any creature), for He would destroy those who committed the sin as well as others of all types of creatures and animals, for the bad consequences of sin may lead to destruction of crops and livestock. (But He defers them for a specified term), He does not hasten the punishment for them until an appointed time, which is the Day of Resurrection. (And when their term has come, they will not remain behind an hour, nor will they precede it), so let them beware, so long as they are still within the respite period before the time comes when there will no longer be any respite. Al-Saadi: 443.\nWhen an individual commits a sin, its harmful consequence can affect the whole society. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَوۡ يُؤَاخِذُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلنَّاسَ بِظُلۡمِهِم مَّا تَرَكَ عَلَيۡهَا مِن دَآبَّةٖ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَخِّرُهُمۡ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗىۖ فَإِذَا جَآءَ أَجَلُهُمۡ لَا يَسۡتَٔۡخِرُونَ سَاعَةٗ وَلَا يَسۡتَقۡدِمُونَ ٦١\nAbu Huraira (t) heard a man saying: \"The wrongdoer does not harm anyone but himself,\" and he replied to him saying: \"Terrible indeed is what you said, the bustard dies in its nest because of the transgression of the wrongdoer.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/620.\nTo what limit the evil consequence of transgression may reach?\nفَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَهُوَ وَلِيُّهُمُ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ ٦٣\nHe is called (their ally) because of their obedience to him. Al-Baghawi: 2/621.\nWhy is satan called (their ally)?\nوَمَآ أَنزَلۡنَا عَلَيۡكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ إِلَّا لِتُبَيِّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلَّذِي ٱخۡتَلَفُواْ فِيهِ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٦٤\nThe primary objectives of the Quran are clearing ignorance, guiding to the knowledge of truth, and materializing the effects of these two objectives, which is the mercy that emerges from avoiding misguidance and following true guidance. Ibn Ashur: 14/196.\nWhat are the primary objectives of revealing the holy Quran?\nwords\nكَظِيمٌSuppressing his anguish\nهُونٍDisgrace\nيَدُسُّهُBuries her\nلا جَرَمَIn fact\nمُفرَطُونَThey will be neglected in Hellfire"],[274,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nDrink milk, then remember how Allah made it for you and say, \"O Allah, bless it for us and give us more of it.\"\nDrink honey today as a means to healing.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from stinginess, laziness; from most decrepit age, the punishment in the grave; from the affliction of Ad-Dajjal (Antichrist), and from the afflictions of life and death.\"\nguid\nIf you reflect on how milk is transformed from fodder plants in the farm to being manufactured in the animal stomach until it becomes a palatable drink on your table, you will not be able to thank Allah enough.\nBeware of envy, as Allah favored some over others in provision and judgement.\nEvery good thing is lawful (Halal), and every bad thing is unlawful (Haram).\nrefl\nوَإِنَّ لَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ لَعِبۡرَةٗۖ\nAbu Bakr Al-Warraq said: \"The lesson in livestock is making them subservient and tamed for their owners while you defy and oppose your Lord in everything; and one of the greatest lessons is that an innocent creature carries a sinning one.\" Al-Qurtubi: 12/350.\nDescribe the lesson that Allah made in livestock?\nوَإِنَّ لَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ لَعِبۡرَةٗۖ نُّسۡقِيكُم مِّمَّا فِي بُطُونِهِۦ مِنۢ بَيۡنِ فَرۡثٖ وَدَمٖ لَّبَنًا خَالِصٗا سَآئِغٗا لِّلشَّٰرِبِينَ ٦٦\nCan this be anything but divine power, not merely the dictates of nature? What a thing in nature that can turn fodder that animals eat and the water they drink, whether it is fresh or salty, into pure milk that is palatable to those who drink it. Al-Saadi: 444.\nWhat is lesson in the flowing of milk from the bellies of livestock?\nوَمِن ثَمَرَٰتِ ٱلنَّخِيلِ وَٱلۡأَعۡنَٰبِ تَتَّخِذُونَ مِنۡهُ سَكَرٗا وَرِزۡقًا حَسَنًاۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٦٧\n(Indeed in that is a sign for a people who reason), understand the perfect might of Allah, as He brings forth provision from trees that are like pieces of lumber, yet they produce delicious fruits. Just as He encompasses all His servants with His mercy, and makes this provision available to them. Al-Saadi: 444.\nWhat are the signs that would benefit the people of reason from the presence of different fruits?\nوَمِن ثَمَرَٰتِ ٱلنَّخِيلِ وَٱلۡأَعۡنَٰبِ تَتَّخِذُونَ مِنۡهُ سَكَرٗا وَرِزۡقًا حَسَنًاۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٦٧\n(You take intoxicant and good provision): Ibn Abbas said: \"Intoxicant is the product of these two fruits that is forbidden, and the good provision is what is permitted of them.\" (Indeed in that is a sign for a people who reason): It is appropriate to mention the reason (intellect) here, because it is the noblest feature of man. Hence, Allah forbade Muslims from drinking intoxicants, in order to protect their ability to reason. Ibn Kathir: 2/556.\nThis verse ends with the mention of the reasoning mind. Why?\nثُمَّ كُلِي مِن كُلِّ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ فَٱسۡلُكِي سُبُلَ رَبِّكِ ذُلُلٗاۚ يَخۡرُجُ مِنۢ بُطُونِهَا شَرَابٞ مُّخۡتَلِفٌ أَلۡوَٰنُهُۥ فِيهِ شِفَآءٞ لِّلنَّاسِۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٦٩\n(Indeed, there is a sign in this for people who reflect), those who contemplate. When contemplating, while using fair judgment, the wonder of the bees, one cannot help but attests that its creator is none but Allah, the Almighty, who inspired the bees this meticulous task with their delicate bodies and ingenious ways of adapting to changing conditions. Moreover, they consume the sour, the bitter, the sweet, the salty, and harmful weeds but in the end, Allah makes it sweet honey and healing for people, which is a clear evidence of His power. Al-Qurtubi: 12/374.\nDescribe one of the wonders about the bees.\nيَخۡرُجُ مِنۢ بُطُونِهَا شَرَابٞ مُّخۡتَلِفٌ أَلۡوَٰنُهُۥ فِيهِ شِفَآءٞ لِّلنَّاسِۚ\nSome of those who spoke about the study of Prophetic medicine said that if [Allah] had said, \"in which there is the healing for people,\" then it would be the remedy for all diseases, but He said, (in which there is healing for people), which is the right treatment for every \"cold\" disease since honey is normally \"hot\", and a disease is be treated with its opposite. Ibn Kathir: 2/556.\nAllah says, (in which there is healing) and not “in which there is the healing.” Why?\nوَٱللَّهُ خَلَقَكُمۡ ثُمَّ يَتَوَفَّىٰكُمۡۚ وَمِنكُم مَّن يُرَدُّ إِلَىٰٓ أَرۡذَلِ ٱلۡعُمُرِ لِكَيۡ لَا يَعۡلَمَ بَعۡدَ عِلۡمٖ شَيۡـًٔاۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلِيمٞ قَدِيرٞ ٧٠\nAnas bin Malik narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to supplicate saying: \"O Allah! I seek refuge with You from stinginess, laziness; from most decrepit age, the punishment in the grave; from the affliction of Ad-Dajjal (Antichrist), and from the afflictions of life and death.\" Al-Alusi: 14/572.\nHow did the Prophet (ﷺ) observe this verse: (Among you are some who are left to reach the most decrepit age)?\nwords\nلَعِبرَةًA lesson\nفَرثٍExcretion in the stomach\nسَائِغًاA pleasant taste\nيَعرِشُونَWhat people construct for beehives\nفَاسلُكِيFollow, enter\nذُلُلًاMade easy for you\nأَرذَلِ العُمُرِThe most decrepit age"],[275,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nPraise Allah for His blessings and provision, then spend from it to charity secretly and openly.\nRemember a relative or a friend of yours who suddenly passed away, and imagine that you will face the same fate.\nReflect on birds and how they fly, and soar high in open air, as your reflection is a response to the command of Allah.\nguid\nWhoever speaks justly and enjoins it, is in a high rank with Allah.\nImagine if one of these faculties: Hearing, sight or intellect become sick or disabled, how will your situation be? Give thanks to Allah for them.\nUse examples in your speech when giving advice and preaching to clarify matters.\nrefl\nفَلَا تَضۡرِبُواْ لِلَّهِ ٱلۡأَمۡثَالَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَعۡلَمُ وَأَنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٧٤\nMeaning: Allah knows the hideousness of your shirk while you do not; but if you did, you would never dare to do it. This is the justification for forbidding you to make comparisons to Him. Or He knows the essence of all things and you do not, so let your view and analogy beneath His revelation. Al-Qasimi: 4/534.\nThe verse ends with (Indeed, Allah knows and you do not know). Why?\nفَلَا تَضۡرِبُواْ لِلَّهِ ٱلۡأَمۡثَالَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَعۡلَمُ وَأَنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٧٤\nThe reason that shirk is making comparisons to Allah is that they attributed divine traits to the idols and likened them to the Creator. Ibn Ashur: 14/223.\nWhy is it wrong and utter ignorance on the part of the polytheists to worship idols?\nضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلًا عَبۡدٗا مَّمۡلُوكٗا لَّا يَقۡدِرُ عَلَىٰ شَيۡءٖ وَمَن رَّزَقۡنَٰهُ مِنَّا رِزۡقًا حَسَنٗا فَهُوَ يُنفِقُ مِنۡهُ سِرّٗا وَجَهۡرًاۖ هَلۡ يَسۡتَوُۥنَۚ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِۚ بَلۡ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٧٥\nAllah compares the inability of their idols to provide them with provision to a bonded slave who is incapable of managing his own affairs, and does not own any wealth. Ibn Ashur: 14/223.\nIdols, shrines, and grave sites are helpless to benefit themselves, so how will they benefit others? Explain in light of this verse.\nضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلًا عَبۡدٗا مَّمۡلُوكٗا لَّا يَقۡدِرُ عَلَىٰ شَيۡءٖ وَمَن رَّزَقۡنَٰهُ مِنَّا رِزۡقًا حَسَنٗا فَهُوَ يُنفِقُ مِنۡهُ سِرّٗا وَجَهۡرًاۖ هَلۡ يَسۡتَوُۥنَۚ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِۚ بَلۡ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٧٥\nThis is an example of Allah, the Almighty, and the idols; the idols are like a helpless bonded slave while Allah, the Almighty, is the King; the provision is in His Hand, and He disposes of it as He wills, so how can He be equated with idols?! Ibn Juzay: 1/432.\nShirk contradicts sound reason. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرَ وَٱلۡأَفۡـِٔدَةَ\nThese three faculties are singled out because of their significance and importance, for they are the key to all knowledge, as no one can acquire knowledge except through one of these three faculties. Al-Saadi: 445.\nWhy are these three faculties singled out for mention?\nأَلَمۡ يَرَوۡاْ إِلَى ٱلطَّيۡرِ مُسَخَّرَٰتٖ فِي جَوِّ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَا يُمۡسِكُهُنَّ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٧٩\nThe term (signs) is in the plural form since there are different indicators of Allah's power in the flight of birds. The creation of air, the suitable bodies of birds to fly in midair, and inspiring birds to float in the air and do not fall to the ground except with their own will. Ibn Ashur: 14/236.\nThe term (signs) is in the plural form. Why?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ\nThe believers are the ones who benefit from the signs of Allah and reflect upon what has been made a sign pointing to Him. As for others, when they look, it is in a heedless and careless manner. Al-Saadi: 445.\nWhy are the believers singed out for benefiting from the universal signs?\nwords\nالأَمثَالَIdols that you associate with Allah\nأَبكَمُDumb, born mute\nكَلٌّHe is a heavy burden\nمَولاهُHis master who takes care of him\nكَلَمحِ البَصَرِLike a blink of an eye, a quick glance"],[276,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nThank Allah for His blessing in providing you with a residence.\nDonate to charity to help a needy person to pay the rent of his residence.\nSay, \"O Allah! I seek refuge in you lest I associate anything with you while I know it, and I seek your forgiveness for what I do not know.\"\nguid\nBe among those who remember and give thanks to Allah for His blessings upon them.\nThe duty of the Messenger (ﷺ) is not guiding people's hearts, rather it is showing the right path by clearly conveying the message.\nSome people will realize the debility of their minds on the Day of Resurrection, which will be too late.\nrefl\nوَٱللَّهُ جَعَلَ لَكُم مِّنۢ بُيُوتِكُمۡ سَكَنٗا وَجَعَلَ لَكُم مِّن جُلُودِ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ بُيُوتٗا تَسۡتَخِفُّونَهَا يَوۡمَ ظَعۡنِكُمۡ وَيَوۡمَ إِقَامَتِكُمۡ وَمِنۡ أَصۡوَافِهَا وَأَوۡبَارِهَا وَأَشۡعَارِهَآ أَثَٰثٗا وَمَتَٰعًا إِلَىٰ حِينٖ ٨٠\nThis enumeration of blessings of which Allah inspired man, such as the blessing of thinking to make protective and embellishing houses, similar garments and furniture in addition to this verse, (And Allah brought you out from your mothers' wombs not knowing anything) [16:78]. They are all part of Allah's kindness that enabled man's mind, and eased the means for him to attain them. Ibn Ashur: 14/236.\nWhat is the link between the above-mentioned verse and this verse: (And Allah brought you out from your mothers' wombs not knowing anything)?\nوَجَعَلَ لَكُمۡ سَرَٰبِيلَ تَقِيكُمُ ٱلۡحَرَّ\nAllah did not mention cold because it was mentioned earlier in this Surah, at the beginning where He mentions basic blessings, which are things that are essential to man; at the end of the Surah, He mentions extra blessings. Protection against the cold is a basic blessing, which is a necessity, and it was mentioned at the beginning of this Surah, where Allah says, (for you as a source of warmth and other benefits) [16:5]. Al-Saadi: 446.\nWhy is (heat) mentioned without the \"cold\" in this verse?\nكَذَٰلِكَ يُتِمُّ نِعۡمَتَهُۥ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\n(This is how He perfects His blessings upon you), Qatadah said: This Surah is called the \"Surah of blessings.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/561.\nSome scholars call this Surah the \"Surah of blessings.\" Why?\nكَذَٰلِكَ يُتِمُّ نِعۡمَتَهُۥ عَلَيۡكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُسۡلِمُونَ ٨١\n(So that) when you remember the blessings of Allah and you see these blessings inundating you from all directions (you may submit to Him) to His greatness, and comply with His commands, and use His blessings to obey the One Who bestowed them and granted them. Abundance of blessings is one of the causes that lead people to show more gratitude and praise Allah for them, but the wrongdoers insist on stubbornly rebelling. Al-Saadi: 446.\nWhen blessings become abundant upon a person, what is his duty toward them?\nيَعۡرِفُونَ نِعۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ يُنكِرُونَهَا وَأَكۡثَرُهُمُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٨٣\n(They recognize the blessings of Allah), this refers to the blessings that are mentioned at the beginning of this Surah up to this verse. (They) the disbelievers who deny Allah's blessings, associate partners with Him, and worship others beside Him. Ibn Juzay: 1/471.\nThe disbelievers admit that Allah is the Creator, the Sustainer, yet they deny His blessings. How?\nثُمَّ لَا يُؤۡذَنُ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَلَا هُمۡ يُسۡتَعۡتَبُونَ ٨٤\nThe disbelievers will not be permitted to make excuses because any excuse they offer, after it becomes certain that what they followed was false, will be an invalid excuse which will not benefit them in the slightest. Al-Saadi: 446.\nOn the Day of Judgment, the disbelievers will not be permitted to make excuses. Why?\nوَإِذَا رَءَا ٱلَّذِينَ أَشۡرَكُواْ شُرَكَآءَهُمۡ قَالُواْ رَبَّنَا هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ شُرَكَآؤُنَا ٱلَّذِينَ كُنَّا نَدۡعُواْ مِن دُونِكَۖ فَأَلۡقَوۡاْ إِلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡقَوۡلَ إِنَّكُمۡ لَكَٰذِبُونَ ٨٦\nsay, \"Our Lord, these are our partners [to You] whom we used to invoke [in worship] besides You.\" But they will throw at them the statement, \"Indeed, you are liars\"]. Meaning: The idols will speak to refute those who worshiped them by stating that they [the idols] were not gods nor did they ask to be worshiped. And so, Allah will make the idols speak in order to disgrace the disbelievers. Al-Qurtubi: 12/409.\nHow will the disbelievers be disgraced with their false gods on the Day of Resurrection?\nwords\nتَستَخِفُّونَهَاYou find light to handle, [tents]\nظَعنِكُمWhen you travel\nوَأَوبَارِهَاCamel's hair, fur\nظِلالًاShades out of what He has created like trees\nسَرَابِيلَGarments"],[277,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nRead a Surah from the Quran and extract three ideas to improve yourself.\nShow kindness to one of your neighbors through a gift or kind words.\nVisit one of your relatives.\nguid\nBe among those who remember and benefit when admonished and reminded of Allah, the Almighty.\nFulfilling your oath and keeping your promise is the path of people of faith.\nStand firm in performing a good deed, and beware of causing it to be nullified and losing its reward.\nrefl\nٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَصَدُّواْ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ زِدۡنَٰهُمۡ عَذَابٗا فَوۡقَ ٱلۡعَذَابِ بِمَا كَانُواْ يُفۡسِدُونَ ٨٨\nMeaning: A punishment for their disbelief and another punishment for turning others away from following the truth. This is a proof that there will be varying levels of punishment for the disbelievers, just as there will be varying degrees of Paradise for the believers. Ibn Kathir: 2/562.\nThis verse indicates varying levels of punishment for the disbelievers in Hellfire. Explain.\nوَيَوۡمَ نَبۡعَثُ فِي كُلِّ أُمَّةٖ شَهِيدًا عَلَيۡهِم مِّنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡۖ وَجِئۡنَا بِكَ شَهِيدًا عَلَىٰ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِۚ\nThe perfect justice of Allah warrants that every Messenger will testify concerning his nation, because he is more aware than others of the deeds of his nation, and he will be more just and too compassionate to testify against them except as they deserve. Al-Saadi: 447.\nIn this verse, there is an indication of the perfect justice and mercy of Allah. Explain.\nوَيَوۡمَ نَبۡعَثُ فِي كُلِّ أُمَّةٖ شَهِيدًا عَلَيۡهِم مِّنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡۖ وَجِئۡنَا بِكَ شَهِيدًا عَلَىٰ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِۚ\n(A witness over them from themselves), this is additional reminding that the testimony of Messengers over their nations cannot be challenged since these witnesses come from them, thus, these nations will not find a way to contest this testimony. Ibn Ashur: 14/250.\nWhat is the benefit of describing the witness as (from themselves)?\nوَنَزَّلۡنَا عَلَيۡكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ تِبۡيَٰنٗا لِّكُلِّ شَيۡءٖ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٗ وَبُشۡرَىٰ لِلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ٨٩\n(For all things), it is comprehensive for which it is intended as Sharia that reforms the souls, completes the standards of morals, rectifies society, clarifies the rights, and what preaching entails of inferring the Oneness of Allah and truthfulness of the Messenger (ﷺ). Ibn Ashur: 14/253.\nThe Holy Quran clarifies what humans need of beliefs, laws, and morals. How?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأۡمُرُ بِٱلۡعَدۡلِ وَٱلۡإِحۡسَٰنِ وَإِيتَآيِٕ ذِي ٱلۡقُرۡبَى\nThis includes all relatives, both close and distant, however, the more closely related they are, the more deserving they are of kindness. Al-Saadi: 447.\nWho are the relatives meant in this verse? Who is more deserving of kindness than others?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأۡمُرُ بِٱلۡعَدۡلِ وَٱلۡإِحۡسَٰنِ وَإِيتَآيِٕ ذِي ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ\nAmong the types of justice and kindness, Allah singles out a type to which most people are heedless and often negligent which is giving help to relatives. Most people concern themselves for non relatives, either to maintain friendship or avoid possible harm from them. Meanwhile, they are completely heedless of their relatives, feeling secure from them, and failing to give what is due to them. Ibn Ashur: 14/256.\nAllah singles out (giving [help] to relatives) after mentioning justice and kindness even though it is included with them. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأۡمُرُ بِٱلۡعَدۡلِ وَٱلۡإِحۡسَٰنِ وَإِيتَآيِٕ ذِي ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ وَيَنۡهَىٰ عَنِ ٱلۡفَحۡشَآءِ وَٱلۡمُنكَرِ وَٱلۡبَغۡيِۚ يَعِظُكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَذَكَّرُونَ ٩٠\nJustice is performing duties while kindness is performing recommended deeds, and these pertain to what is due to Allah and what is due to the people. Ibn Masoud (t) said: \"This is the most comprehensive verse in the Book of Allah.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/472.\nWhy is this verse considered the most comprehensive verse in the Book of Allah?\nwords\nالفَحشَاءِShameful acts, ugly lies\nوَالبَغيِTransgression and oppression\nكَفِيلًاA guarantor and witness\nأَنكَاثًاUnknits into shreds after weaving\nدَخَلًاDeceit\nأَربَىMore plentiful in wealth and benefit"],[278,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nGive to charity in the hope of gaining its benefit and blessing in this world and on the Day of Resurrection.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the accursed devil when you recite the Quran, especially when reciting Al-Fatiha in prayer.\nAsk Allah, the Almighty, to make you one of his servants over whom the devil has no power.\nguid\nOne of Allah's blessings upon a patient believer is that on the Day of Resurrection, He will look at his best deed and make him worthy of its reward for all other good deeds, even if he only did it once in his life.\nFaith and reliance upon Allah, the Almighty, are two reasons for protection from the evils of the devil and his whispers.\nReciting the Quran often is one of the reasons for steadfastness in the religion of Allah.\nrefl\nمَا عِندَكُمۡ يَنفَدُ وَمَا عِندَ ٱللَّهِ بَاقٖۗ\nHence, give precedence to what will abide over what will cease to be, for whatever you have, even if you have a great deal, will inevitably come to an end and will perish, but what Allah has is everlasting as He is, so it will never cease to be or perish. Therefore, he is not wise who gives precedence to what is transient and insignificant over what will abide and is precious. This offers encouragement to be uninterested in worldly matters, especially the disinterest in what is harmful. Al-Saadi: 448-449.\nFor a wise Muslim, what lesson can be learned from this verse?\nمَنۡ عَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا مِّن ذَكَرٍ أَوۡ أُنثَىٰ وَهُوَ مُؤۡمِنٞ فَلَنُحۡيِيَنَّهُۥ حَيَوٰةٗ طَيِّبَةٗۖ\nTherefore, faith is a condition of the validity and acceptance of righteous deeds. In fact, a deed cannot be called righteous unless it is done on the basis of faith, and the faith which inspires one to do good deeds is certain faith that leads to physical actions, both obligatory and recommended. Al-Saadi: 449.\nAllah stipulates faith as a condition for accepting righteous deeds. Why?\nمَنۡ عَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا مِّن ذَكَرٍ أَوۡ أُنثَىٰ وَهُوَ مُؤۡمِنٞ فَلَنُحۡيِيَنَّهُۥ حَيَوٰةٗ طَيِّبَةٗۖ وَلَنَجۡزِيَنَّهُمۡ أَجۡرَهُم بِأَحۡسَنِ مَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٩٧\nAllah links happiness (good life) to faith and doing righteous deeds. Ibn Taimyah: 4/176.\nIn this verse, happiness is linked to two things, what are they?\nفَإِذَا قَرَأۡتَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ فَٱسۡتَعِذۡ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ ٩٨\nThe reason for seeking refuge with Allah before reciting is that the reader should not get confused or mixed up, and that satan would not confuse him or stop him from thinking about and reflecting on the meaning of what he recites. Ibn Kathir: 2/566.\nThe verse mentions a good way to help the reader reflect on the Holy Quran?\nإِنَّهُۥ لَيۡسَ لَهُۥ سُلۡطَٰنٌ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ ٩٩\nIt means that satan has no power over the believers, and cannot misguide them. Ibn Juzay: 1/473.\nWhat are the traits that you should attain so that satan cannot have power over you?\nإِنَّهُۥ لَيۡسَ لَهُۥ سُلۡطَٰنٌ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ ٩٩\nSufyan Al-Thawri said: \"satan has no power to make the believers commit a sin that they will not repent from.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/566.\nWhat is the negated authority of satan over the believers?\nإِنَّهُۥ لَيۡسَ لَهُۥ سُلۡطَٰنٌ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ ٩٩\nThe negation of satan's power is conditional upon two things: Faith and reliance upon Allah. Ibn Ashur: 14/278.\nWhat prevents satan from having power over man?\nwords\nيَنفَدُIt comes to an end, perishes\nالرَّجِيمِThe accursed\nسُلطَانٌPower, authority\nيَتَوَلَّونَهُThey take him as an ally\nمُفتَرٍAn inventor of lies\nرُوحُ القُدُسِThe holy spirit: the angel Gabriel"],[279,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nTake part in defending the religion and its people on the Internet or on social media.\nPay a visit to a graveyard and reflect on your first night in the grave.\nDraw three useful lessons from the verse.\nguid\nLearning the Arabic language is a act of worship because it eases the understanding of the Holy Quran.\nGiving in to the pursuit of worldly pleasures is a cause of deviation.\nOne of the signs of heedlessness is not adhering to admonishments and reminding nor trying to benefit from them.\nrefl\nإِنَّمَا يَفۡتَرِي ٱلۡكَذِبَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡكَٰذِبُونَ ١٠٥\nThis is a response to their claim: (You are an inventor of lies) [16:101], which means that inventing lies befits those who do not believe since they lack the fear of Allah, but for one who believes in Allah will never lie about Him. Ibn Juzay: 1/474.\nFaith contravenes lying, explain in light of this verse.\nمَن كَفَرَ بِٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ إِيمَٰنِهِۦٓ إِلَّا مَنۡ أُكۡرِهَ وَقَلۡبُهُۥ مُطۡمَئِنُّۢ بِٱلۡإِيمَٰنِ\nWhoever is forced and compelled to disbelieve but his heart remains steadfast in faith and he wants to believe, there is no blame or sin on him. Al-Saadi: 450.\nWhen true compulsion is present, then Allah's mercy is vast. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَٰكِن مَّن شَرَحَ بِٱلۡكُفۡرِ صَدۡرٗا فَعَلَيۡهِمۡ غَضَبٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٞ ١٠٦\nAllah states that He is angry with those who -after pondering and accepting faith- became disbelievers and open their hearts to disbelief finding peace in that. They deserve Allah's wrath because they understood the faith yet still they turned away from it. Ibn Kathir: 2/568.\nThe sin of an apostate is worse than that of one who is a disbeliever from the outset. Why?\nمَن كَفَرَ بِٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ إِيمَٰنِهِۦٓ إِلَّا مَنۡ أُكۡرِهَ وَقَلۡبُهُۥ مُطۡمَئِنُّۢ بِٱلۡإِيمَٰنِ وَلَٰكِن مَّن شَرَحَ بِٱلۡكُفۡرِ صَدۡرٗا فَعَلَيۡهِمۡ غَضَبٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٞ ١٠٦\nThere is consensus among scholars that whoever was compelled to disbelieve but chose death instead, has a greater reward than that of one who decided to take the exemption. Al-Qurtubi: 12/444.\nWhat are the options for a believer to take during a state of duress, starting with the best?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمُ ٱسۡتَحَبُّواْ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا عَلَى ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ١٠٧\nThey left the faith for the sake of this world since they preferred this life to the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 2/568.\nThe verse indicates a major cause for apostasy. What is it?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمُ ٱسۡتَحَبُّواْ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا عَلَى ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ١٠٧\nAllah, the Almighty, ascertains that favoring the life of this world over the Hereafter is the fundamental cause for the manifest loss. Ibn Taimyah: 4/185.\nWhat is the fundamental cause for the misguidance of disbelievers?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ طَبَعَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ وَسَمۡعِهِمۡ وَأَبۡصَٰرِهِمۡۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡغَٰفِلُونَ ١٠٨\nAllah describes them as: (These are the ones whose hearts, hearing and sight are sealed up), which means that their hearts are sealed against understanding admonishments; (hearing) sealed against listening to the words of Allah; (sight) sealed against seeing the signs; (it is they who are the heedless), heedless of what will happen to them. Al-Qurtubi: 12/449.\nWhat are the effects of sealing on hearts, sights, and hearings?\nwords\nيُلحِدُونَ إِلَيهِThey claim that a non-Arab used to teach the Prophet (ﷺ)\nطَبَعَHe has put a seal\nلا جَرَمَIn fact\nفُتِنُواThey were persecuted and tortured"],[280,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nWork on your shortcomings by reflecting on them and knowing how to rectify them.\nShare a message in which you warn against examples of ingratitude for blessings in the society.\nMention the Name of Allah before you eat, and praise Him afterward, and when you have edible leftovers, give them to someone in need.\nguid\nReflect on the reasons behind Allah's destruction of nations, old and current.\nDo not eat anything on which Allah's name has not been mentioned, and beware of the food processing companies’ lies [that it may be halal], as this is a reason for your supplications to be unanswered, and you being distant from your Lord.\nIf a preacher or an advisor comes to you, accept the truth from him in submission to Allah's commands.\nrefl\nيَوْمَ تَأْتِى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ تُجَٰدِلُ عَن نَّفْسِهَا وَتُوَفَّىٰ كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ مَّا عَمِلَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُونَ ١١١\n(On the Day when each soul will come pleading for itself), arguing and protesting for himself over what he had done of good and evil deeds; totally occupied with himself and not concerned about others. Al-Baghawi: 2/641.\nWhen will a person be totally occupied with himself and not concerned about others?\nوَضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلًا قَرْيَةً كَانَتْ ءَامِنَةً مُّطْمَئِنَّةً يَأْتِيهَا رِزْقُهَا رَغَدًا مِّن كُلِّ مَكَانٍۢ فَكَفَرَتْ بِأَنْعُمِ ٱللَّهِ فَأَذَٰقَهَا ٱللَّهُ لِبَاسَ ٱلْجُوعِ وَٱلْخَوْفِ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَصْنَعُونَ ١١٢\nIn this verse, safety precedes security since security does not exist without safety, moreover, fear causes anxiety and worry. Ibn Ashur: 14/305.\nIn this verse, safety precedes security. Why?\nوَضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلًا قَرْيَةً كَانَتْ ءَامِنَةً مُّطْمَئِنَّةً يَأْتِيهَا رِزْقُهَا رَغَدًا مِّن كُلِّ مَكَانٍۢ فَكَفَرَتْ بِأَنْعُمِ ٱللَّهِ فَأَذَٰقَهَا ٱللَّهُ لِبَاسَ ٱلْجُوعِ وَٱلْخَوْفِ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَصْنَعُونَ ١١٢\nIn the original Arabic text, it is called \"the garment of hunger and fear\" because feebleness, paleness, and misery were clearly showing on them like a garment. Al-Qurtubi: 12/452.\nAllah calls the hunger and fear by which destroyed nations were punished a garment. Why?\nوَضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلًا قَرْيَةً كَانَتْ ءَامِنَةً مُّطْمَئِنَّةً يَأْتِيهَا رِزْقُهَا رَغَدًا مِّن كُلِّ مَكَانٍۢ فَكَفَرَتْ بِأَنْعُمِ ٱللَّهِ فَأَذَٰقَهَا ٱللَّهُ لِبَاسَ ٱلْجُوعِ وَٱلْخَوْفِ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَصْنَعُونَ ١١٢\nAllah made them an example and an admonishment to those who would show the same ingratitude for His favors. Ibn Ashur: 14/303.\nHow do destroyed cities become an example and an admonishment to others?\nإِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡمَيۡتَةَ وَٱلدَّمَ وَلَحۡمَ ٱلۡخِنزِيرِ وَمَآ أُهِلَّ لِغَيۡرِ ٱللَّهِ بِهِۦۖ\nAllah has only forbidden impure things to us by His grace, to protect us from everything that is repellent. Al-Saadi: 451.\nWhat is the reason for the prohibition of some food items?\nوَلَا تَقُولُواْ لِمَا تَصِفُ أَلۡسِنَتُكُمُ ٱلۡكَذِبَ هَٰذَا حَلَٰلٞ وَهَٰذَا حَرَامٞ لِّتَفۡتَرُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَفۡتَرُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَ لَا يُفۡلِحُونَ ١١٦\nThis includes anyone who comes up with an innovation in religion (Bid'ah) for which he has no evidence from Sharia. Ibn Kathir: 2/570.\nThis verse indicates the prohibition of innovation in religious matters. How?\nوَلَا تَقُولُواْ لِمَا تَصِفُ أَلۡسِنَتُكُمُ ٱلۡكَذِبَ هَٰذَا حَلَٰلٞ وَهَٰذَا حَرَامٞ لِّتَفۡتَرُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَفۡتَرُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَ لَا يُفۡلِحُونَ ١١٦\nThis verse addresses the Arabs who were -during the times of ignorance- used to make some things lawful and other things unlawful, such as Al-Bahira [a she-camel whose milk was spared for the sake of the idols] and others that are mentioned in Surahs, Al-Ma'idah and Al-An'am. Moreover, this verse includes anyone who says, (This is lawful) and (This is unlawful) without proper knowledge. Ibn Juzay: 1/476.\nWhat are the categories of people included in this verse?\nwords\nرَغَدًاEasy and in abundance\nغَيرَ بَاغٍNot driven by desire nor pursuing the unlawful\nوَلا عَادٍNot exceeding the need"],[281,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nFrom this verse, extract the methods of inviting others to Allah and apply them today.\nPractice arguing with a friend today in the best manner.\nRecall a sin that you had committed out of ignorance, and ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nSome methods of inviting others to Allah are through wisdom, goodly exhortation, and arguing with them in the best manner.\nIf Allah intends good for a servant, He grants him patience.\nPiety and doing good are two causes for a servant to be in Allah's care.\nrefl\nثُمَّ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ لِلَّذِينَ عَمِلُواْ ٱلسُّوٓءَ بِجَهَٰلَةٖ ثُمَّ تَابُواْ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ذَٰلِكَ وَأَصۡلَحُوٓاْ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهَا لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٌ ١١٩\nAllah states that due to His bestowing of graciousness and favor upon the believers who have sinned that whoever among them repents, Allah will accept his repentance, as He says, (Then, indeed, your Lord, to those who have done wrong out of ignorance). Some of the righteous predecessors said: It means that whoever disobeys Allah is ignorant. Ibn Kathir: 2/571.\nWhy is a sinner described as ignorant?\nثُمَّ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ لِلَّذِينَ عَمِلُواْ ٱلسُّوٓءَ بِجَهَٰلَةٖ ثُمَّ تَابُواْ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ذَٰلِكَ وَأَصۡلَحُوٓاْ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهَا لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٌ ١١٩\nCorrecting one's self means steadfastness in repentance. Al-Baghawi: 2/643.\nWhat is meant by (and then repent after that and correct themselves)?\nإِنَّ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ كَانَ أُمَّةٗ قَانِتٗا لِّلَّهِ حَنِيفٗا وَلَمۡ يَكُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١٢٠\n(Indeed, Abraham was Ummah), there are two possible meanings: First: Abraham (u) was Ummah on his own because he possessed all the good righteous qualities. Second: Abraham (u) was Ummah in the sense that he was an exemplary leader, as Allah says, (Indeed, I will make you a leader for mankind) [2:124]. Ibn Masoud (t) said: Ummah is the one who teaches people what is good. Ibn Juzay: 1/477.\nThe term (Ummah) implies many traits of Abraham (u), what are they?\nوَلَمۡ يَكُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١٢٠\nAllah denies that Abraham (u) was a polytheist in response to Arab polytheists who affiliate themselves with him. Ibn Juzay: 1/477\nFor someone who affiliates himself with the Prophet (ﷺ) or his family, does that benefit him?\nٱدۡعُ إِلَىٰ سَبِيلِ رَبِّكَ بِٱلۡحِكۡمَةِ وَٱلۡمَوۡعِظَةِ ٱلۡحَسَنَةِۖ وَجَٰدِلۡهُم بِٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦ وَهُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِٱلۡمُهۡتَدِينَ ١٢٥\n(The way of your Lord) is Islam, (wisdom) is saying the right words, and (goodly preaching) is exhortation and intimidation. Arguing is responding to the opponent. These three methods are called by mental scientists: Proof, speech, and argument. Ibn Juzay: 1/478.\nIn light of this verse, discuss the fundamentals of successful preaching.\nوَجَٰدِلۡهُم بِٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُۚ\nThe one who invites others to the way of Allah should reason with them in the most courteous manner. These are the ways that are more likely to bring a response, according to both reason and the texts. One way of doing that is to use evidence that they believe is sound, because this is more likely to achieve the goal and not lead to dispute or trading of insults, which will defeat the purpose and will be of no benefit. Rather, the aim is to guide people to the truth, not to be confrontational and the like. Al-Saadi: 452.\nHow can arguing in the best manner be achieved?\nوَٱصۡبِرۡ وَمَا صَبۡرُكَ إِلَّا بِٱللَّهِۚ\nMeaning: Your patience is attained only with Allah's help and guidance. Al-Baghawi: 2/647.\nCan a servant achieve patience on his own?\nwords\nبِجَهَالَةٍOut of ignorance\nأُمَّةًA comprehensive leader\nقَانِتًاDevoutly obedient to Allah\nحَنِيفًاInclining toward truth\nاجتَبَاهُAllah chose him\nسَبِيلِ رَبِّكَThe religion and straight path of your Lord"],[282,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nSay, \"Glory be to Allah\", and repeat it often, as it signifies veneration of Allah, the Almighty, and it is the most beloved words to Him. Moreover, it is the exaltation of Allah which is unique to Him.\nMeet in a group with some of your friends or brethren and read about the event of Isra' and Miraj (night Journey and the ascension into Heavens) from Sahih Al-Bukhari or the interpretation of the Quran by Ibn Kathir.\nThink of five of the biggest blessings of Allah upon you, and thank Him so that you follow the example of the Prophets in their gratitude to Allah.\nguid\nTake Allah, the Almighty, as a Disposer of all your affairs.\nWhat Allah decrees will happen, what He promises will be fulfilled, and the belief in that is an obligation.\nBeing grateful is an attribute of Allah's Messengers, so follow their guidance.\nrefl\nسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَسۡرَىٰ بِعَبۡدِهِۦ لَيۡلٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ إِلَى ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡأَقۡصَا ٱلَّذِي بَٰرَكۡنَا حَوۡلَهُۥ لِنُرِيَهُۥ مِنۡ ءَايَٰتِنَآۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡبَصِيرُ ١\nThis verse starts with the glorification of Allah without stating anything above which glorifying Allah was done. This indicates that extraordinary news is about to be relayed to the listeners with regards the great might of the speaker and the high rank of the spoken about. Ibn Ashur: 15/9.\nThis verse starts with the glorification of Allah. Why?\nسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَسۡرَىٰ بِعَبۡدِهِۦ لَيۡلٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ إِلَى ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡأَقۡصَا\nThe truth is that the Prophet (ﷺ) was taken on the night journey when he was awake, not in a dream. The glorification of Allah is spoken in the case of serious matters. If it had been a dream, it would not have been a significant matter nor would it be so astounding; the disbelievers of the Quraysh would not have hastened to label him a liar and the group of people who had become Muslims would not have deserted the faith. The term (His slave), refers to both soul and body, and Allah says, (took His slave [Muhammad] by night). Ibn Kathir: 3/23.\nWas the soul of the Prophet (ﷺ) taken on the night journey or his soul and body? Explain.\nسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَسۡرَىٰ بِعَبۡدِهِۦ\nAllah refers to the Prophet (ﷺ) here as (His slave), because he attained all that he attained of high ranks by virtue of perfecting his submission to his Lord. Al-Saadi: 453.\nWhat is the wisdom behind describing the Prophet (ﷺ) as (His slave)?\nوَءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَى ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَجَعَلۡنَٰهُ هُدٗى لِّبَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ أَلَّا تَتَّخِذُواْ مِن دُونِي وَكِيلٗا ٢\nAllah forbids the taking of anyone beside Him as a Disposer of affairs because any created being cannot fulfill all the needs of the servant. The permissible disposing of affairs is to delegate someone to perform a certain task within his ability, thus, the client gains some of his needs, however, no one can satisfy all of his needs except Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 4/202.\nAllah forbids the taking of anyone beside Him as a Disposer of affairs. Why?\nذُرِّيَّةَ مَنۡ حَمَلۡنَا مَعَ نُوحٍۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ عَبۡدٗا شَكُورٗا ٣\nMeaning: Noah (u) was very grateful to Allah for all things. This is an explanation of the preceding verse: Be grateful to Allah as your father Noah (u) was. Ibn Juzay: 1/481.\nAmong Noah's (u) traits, Allah singles out his gratitude. Why?\nفَإِذَا جَآءَ وَعۡدُ أُولَىٰهُمَا بَعَثۡنَا عَلَيۡكُمۡ عِبَادٗا لَّنَآ أُوْلِي بَأۡسٖ شَدِيدٖ فَجَاسُواْ خِلَٰلَ ٱلدِّيَارِۚ وَكَانَ وَعۡدٗا مَّفۡعُولٗا ٥ ثُمَّ رَدَدۡنَا لَكُمُ ٱلۡكَرَّةَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَأَمۡدَدۡنَٰكُم بِأَمۡوَٰلٖ وَبَنِينَ وَجَعَلۡنَٰكُمۡ أَكۡثَرَ نَفِيرًا ٦\nThe victory of the children of Israel over their enemies at times and their defeat against them at other times is a sign of the Prophethood of Moses (u). Moreover, the victory of Muslims over their enemies at times and their defeat against them at other times is a sign of the Prophethood of Muhammad (ﷺ). Ibn Taimyah: 4/203.\nThese verses indicate the victory of the children of Israel over their enemies at times and their defeat against them at other times. What can be inferred from that?\nإِنۡ أَحۡسَنتُمۡ أَحۡسَنتُمۡ لِأَنفُسِكُمۡۖ وَإِنۡ أَسَأۡتُمۡ فَلَهَاۚ\n(If you do good, it is for your own good), which means that We gave you the upper hand over them because of your repentance and the coming of a new generation, so you are in a blessed state. If you do good, you will be recompensed the same, but if you do evil, it is to your own loss. Just as We destroyed those before you because of their sins, We have dealt with you in kindness because of your repentance, so beware of doing evil, lest you end up like them. Ibn Ashur: 15/28.\nThis verse contains glad tidings and a warning. What is the warning about?\nwords\nوَكِيلًاA deity whom you entrust your affairs to Him\nفَجَاسُواThey probed, moved freely\nالكَرَّةَVictory, the upper hand\nوَلِيُتَبِّرُواSo they to destroy\nتَتبِيرًاUtter destruction"],[283,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nIdentify a matter which concerns you, then search for verses in the Quran that pertain to it, and follow their guidance so that Allah may ease it for you.\nSupplicate Allah to make you and your family righteous.\nShare a message in which you explain the risk of extravagance and its bad consequences.\nguid\nBeware of praying for evil against yourself, children or wealth.\nDo not go against the natural disposition by working at night and sleeping during the day.\nThe wickedness and defiant disobedience of others may become a cause for destroying you and those around you if you do not enjoin what is right and forbid what is evil.\nrefl\nعَسَىٰ رَبُّكُمۡ أَن يَرۡحَمَكُمۡۚ وَإِنۡ عُدتُّمۡ عُدۡنَاۚ وَجَعَلۡنَا جَهَنَّمَ لِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ حَصِيرًا ٨\nThese verses contain a warning for the Muslim Ummah against committing sins, lest there befall them what befell the Children of Israel, for the way of Allah [in dealing with sinners] is the same and never changes or alters. Anyone who examines how the disbelievers and wrongdoers have the upper hand over the Muslims will realize that this is a punishment to them because of their sins; if they adhere to the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger (ﷺ), Allah will establish them in the land and grant them victory over their enemies. Al-Saadi: 454.\nWhen reciting a verse that narrates the story of another nation, how do you benefit from that for inviting others to Allah?\nإِنَّ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ يَهۡدِي لِلَّتِي هِيَ أَقۡوَمُ وَيُبَشِّرُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ أَنَّ لَهُمۡ أَجۡرٗا كَبِيرٗا ٩\nMeaning: The Quran guides to what is most upright more so than the guidance of the Scripture of the Children of Israel which is mentioned earlier, (and made it a guidance for the Children of Israel). It indicates that the Ummah of the Quran is safe from deviating from the most upright way. Ibn Ashur: 15/4.\nThe Holy Quran is a safeguard against deviation. How is this inferred from the verse?\nوَيَدۡعُ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ بِٱلشَّرِّ دُعَآءَهُۥ بِٱلۡخَيۡرِۖ وَكَانَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ عَجُولٗا ١١\nIbn Abbas (t) and others said: This is praying against oneself and children at times of distress for things which that he does not really like to be answered. Al-Qurtubi: 13/34.\nGive an example of man's hastiness.\nوَيَدۡعُ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ بِٱلشَّرِّ دُعَآءَهُۥ بِٱلۡخَيۡرِۖ وَكَانَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ عَجُولٗا ١١\nThis is a censure and a reproach for what people do at times of anger when they invoke Allah against themselves, their properties and children; they pray for evil during times of frustration similar to when they pray for good at times of sanity. Ibn Juzay: 1/483.\nSome people may cause harm to themselves. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَجَعَلۡنَا ٱلَّيۡلَ وَٱلنَّهَارَ ءَايَتَيۡنِۖ فَمَحَوۡنَآ ءَايَةَ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَجَعَلۡنَآ ءَايَةَ ٱلنَّهَارِ مُبۡصِرَةٗ لِّتَبۡتَغُواْ فَضۡلٗا مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ وَلِتَعۡلَمُواْ عَدَدَ ٱلسِّنِينَ وَٱلۡحِسَابَۚ وَكُلَّ شَيۡءٖ فَصَّلۡنَٰهُ تَفۡصِيلٗا ١٢\nMeaning: Two signs indicating the Oneness of Allah, His existence, His perfect knowledge and power. The sign is in the fact that, for an observer, each one of them begins from the unknown and fades into the unknown. Moreover, the decrease in either one is an increase to the other, and the brightness of the day as opposed to the darkness of the night. Al-Qurtubi: 13/37.\nWhy are the night and day considered to be signs?\nٱقۡرَأۡ كِتَٰبَكَ كَفَىٰ بِنَفۡسِكَ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ عَلَيۡكَ حَسِيبٗا ١٤\nThis is the ultimate justice and fairness, that it will be said to the individual: \"Take account of your self\", thus he will acknowledge his wrongdoing that brought the punishment upon him. Al-Saadi: 455.\nIn light of this verse, discuss the perfect justice of Allah, the Almighty.\nوَكَمۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَا مِنَ ٱلۡقُرُونِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ نُوحٖۗ\nMeaning: You disbelievers are not dearer to Allah than they were, and you have rejected the noblest of the Messengers and the best of creation, so you are more deserving of punishment. Ibn Kathir: 3/33.\nWhat is the aim of informing that Allah had destroyed many nations after the people of Noah (u)?\nwords\nحَصِيرًاA prison with no way out\nأَقوَمُThe most fair and upright\nفَمَحَونَاWe erased\nمُبصِرَةًA visible\nطَائِرَهُHis deeds (good and evil)\nوَلا تَزِرُAnd will not bear\nوَازِرَةٌA soul that is bearer of burdens"],[284,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nPresent your parents with a gift today and say something they like.\nVisit some relatives today or call them, or give charity to a needy person.\nShare a message in which you explain the risk of spending wastefully.\nguid\nA mere desire for the Hereafter is not enough, for there must be faith and good deeds to go along with that desire.\nAllah, the Almighty, bestows wealth upon those He loves and those He does not, and His giving is either for honoring, testing, or gradually leading to doom.\nDo not forget that you will be held accountable for your wealth.\nrefl\nثُمَّ جَعَلۡنَا لَهُۥ جَهَنَّمَ يَصۡلَىٰهَا مَذۡمُومٗا مَّدۡحُورٗا ١٨\nMeaning: He will be in a state of disgrace, shame and condemnation from Allah and from His created beings, far removed from the mercy of Allah. So, punishment and disgrace will be combined for him. Al-Saadi: 455.\nThe punishment in Hellfire will be both physical and mental. Explain in the light of this verse.\nوَمَنۡ أَرَادَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَ وَسَعَىٰ لَهَا سَعۡيَهَا وَهُوَ مُؤۡمِنٞ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ كَانَ سَعۡيُهُم مَّشۡكُورٗا ١٩\nThis verse alerts to the fact that desiring the Hereafter without striving for it is a mere delusion. Desiring anything must be accompanied by pursuing the means to achieve it. Ibn Ashur: 15/60.\nIt is considered heedlessness and delusional to desire good things, yet, you do not pursue the means to achieve them. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَقَضَىٰ رَبُّكَ أَلَّا تَعۡبُدُوٓاْ إِلَّآ إِيَّاهُ وَبِٱلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ إِحۡسَٰنًاۚ إِمَّا يَبۡلُغَنَّ عِندَكَ ٱلۡكِبَرَ أَحَدُهُمَآ أَوۡ كِلَاهُمَا فَلَا تَقُل لَّهُمَآ أُفّٖ وَلَا تَنۡهَرۡهُمَا وَقُل لَّهُمَا قَوۡلٗا كَرِيمٗا ٢٣\nThe old age of parents is mentioned because that is when they need kindness and care more than ever due to their weakness. Ibn Juzay: 1/485.\nAllah singles out parents' old age for more kindness even though it is obligated at all times. Why?\nوَقَضَىٰ رَبُّكَ أَلَّا تَعۡبُدُوٓاْ إِلَّآ إِيَّاهُ وَبِٱلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ إِحۡسَٰنًاۚ إِمَّا يَبۡلُغَنَّ عِندَكَ ٱلۡكِبَرَ أَحَدُهُمَآ أَوۡ كِلَاهُمَا فَلَا تَقُل لَّهُمَآ أُفّٖ وَلَا تَنۡهَرۡهُمَا وَقُل لَّهُمَا قَوۡلٗا كَرِيمٗا ٢٣\n(Uff) is a word of annoyance which is usually said at times of irritation, etc., but what is meant is the least dislikable word uttered by people. Since Allah forbids saying such words to parents, then what is considered worse than these words is even more prohibited. Ibn Juzay: 1/485.\nThe prohibition of saying the word (uff) implies a stern warning to the offspring. Explain.\nوَقُل رَّبِّ ٱرۡحَمۡهُمَا كَمَا رَبَّيَانِي صَغِيرٗا ٢٤\nFrom this, it is understood that the longer they take care of you, the more rights they have over you. Similarly, if someone other than the parents takes care of a person with regard to his religious and worldly interests, and shows him the right path in a sound manner, that person is indebted to the one who took care of him. Al-Saadi: 456.\nWe often hear: the teacher is like a second father, then, what is the teacher's deserved right?\nوَقُل رَّبِّ ٱرۡحَمۡهُمَا كَمَا رَبَّيَانِي صَغِيرٗا ٢٤\nAllah mentions the \"bringing up\" so that the servant will always remember the compassion and tiredness of his parents in bringing him up, which will increase his tenderness and kindness toward them. Al-Qurtubi: 13/60.\nWhat is the aim of mentioning parents bringing up of their son when he was a child?\nوَلَا تُبَذِّرۡ تَبۡذِيرًا ٢٦ إِنَّ ٱلۡمُبَذِّرِينَ كَانُوٓاْ إِخۡوَٰنَ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينِۖ وَكَانَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ لِرَبِّهِۦ كَفُورٗا ٢٧\nWhoever spends his wealth on desires that are beyond his needs and risks losing his wealth is a wasteful spender. Al-Qurtubi: 13/65.\nWhen is the servant considered to be a wasteful spender?\nwords\nالعَاجِلَةَThis worldly life\nمَدحُورًاBanished from Allah's mercy\nمَحظُورًاRestricted\nمَخذُولًاForsaken\nلِلأَوَّابِينَThose who constantly turn to Allah"],[285,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nIdentify a cause that reminds you of disobedience and keep away from it.\nSponsor an orphan or participate in his sponsorship through a charitable institution.\nFor all things that you have no knowledge of, always say, \"I do not know\", \"I am not aware.\"\nguid\nKeep away from the steps that lead to committing shameful acts and disobediences, as whoever lets his flocks graze around the protected area will soon find his flocks transgressing upon it.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, you will be held accountable for the covenants and contracts that you made with Allah or the people, so make sure you fulfill them.\nYou will be held responsible for the use of your faculties, for the only one who appreciates their true value is he who lost them, so use them for Allah's obedience.\nrefl\nوَلَا تَجۡعَلۡ يَدَكَ مَغۡلُولَةً إِلَىٰ عُنُقِكَ وَلَا تَبۡسُطۡهَا كُلَّ ٱلۡبَسۡطِ فَتَقۡعُدَ مَلُومٗا مَّحۡسُورًا ٢٩\n(And do not make your hand [as] chained to your neck), this is a metaphor for stinginess, where a stingy person is similar to one whose hands are stopped spending and held in chains to his neck. (Or extend it completely), this is a metaphor for extreme spending. So, Allah forbids taking either of these two extremes and enjoins a balanced approach as He says, (And those who neither spend wastefully nor stingily, but are moderate between them) [25:67]. Ibn Juzay: 1/486.\nAllah made Islamic Sharia a balanced one. Give an example.\nإِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَبۡسُطُ ٱلرِّزۡقَ لِمَن يَشَآءُ وَيَقۡدِرُۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهِۦ خَبِيرَۢا بَصِيرٗا ٣٠\nMeaning: Allah knows and sees who deserves to be rich and who deserves to be poor. Some people are more susceptible to corruption if they become rich, thus, a lack of wealth suits them better. Others are just the opposite, poverty may weaken their faith, and thus, wealth suits them better. In some cases, wealth may be decreed for someone leading him to his doom. In other cases, poverty may be a punishment. We seek refuge with Allah from both. Ibn Kathir: 3/37.\nThis verse concludes with Allah's Names: (All-Aware) and (All-Seeing) Why?\nوَلَا تَقۡتُلُوٓاْ أَوۡلَٰدَكُمۡ خَشۡيَةَ إِمۡلَٰقٖۖ\nThis verse indicates that Allah is more compassionate toward His servants than a father to his child. Ibn Kathir: 3/37.\nWho has more compassion for you: your Lord or your parents? And why?\nوَلَا تَقۡرَبُواْ ٱلزِّنَىٰٓۖ\nThe prohibition of going near the matter is more eloquent than the prohibition on simply doing it, because this includes the prohibition of all precursors that lead to it, for whoever lets his flocks graze around the protected area will soon find his flocks transgressing upon it. This is especially applicable regarding this matter, as many people have the strongest inclination toward it. Al-Saadi: 457.\nWhat is the difference between: (do not go near adultery) and \"do not commit adultery\"? Which statement is more eloquent and stronger in prohibition?\nوَلَا تَقۡرَبُواْ ٱلزِّنَىٰٓۖ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فَٰحِشَةٗ وَسَآءَ سَبِيلٗا ٣٢\nDue to its abhorrent nature, Allah describes fornication (adultery) as a shameful act, which means a sin that is regarded as shameful and evil according to Islamic teachings, intellect and human nature, because it involves a transgression of the sacred limits set by Allah, and it is also a transgression against the woman and against her family or husband, it causes trouble in marriages, mixes lineages, and leads to other negative consequences. Al-Saadi: 457.\nWhat are the reasons for describing adultery as a shameful act?\nوَلَا تَقۡفُ مَا لَيۡسَ لَكَ بِهِۦ عِلۡمٌۚ إِنَّ ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَٱلۡبَصَرَ وَٱلۡفُؤَادَ كُلُّ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ كَانَ عَنۡهُ مَسۡـُٔولٗا ٣٦\nThis is a great moral etiquette and a valuable reform of the mind that teaches the Muslim Ummah the difference between the levels of thoughts of the mind so that the known, the suspected, and the illusionary do not become mixed up with each other. Ibn Ashur: 15/101.\nThis verse contains a moral etiquette and a valuable reform of the mind. Explain.\nإِنَّكَ لَن تَخۡرِقَ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ وَلَن تَبۡلُغَ ٱلۡجِبَالَ طُولٗا ٣٧\nMeaning: Your ability will not reach that, in fact, you are a humble servant who is surrounded from above and below. A surrounded person is confined and weak, thus, arrogance does not befit you. Al-Qurtubi: 13/83.\nWhy is arrogance not befitting for a weak slave?\nwords\nمَلُومًاBlamed and censured by others\nمَحسُورًاInsolvent\nوَيَقدِرُRestricts\nإِملاقٍPoverty\nوَلا تَقفُDo not pursue\nمَرَحًاArrogantly"],[286,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nRead a Surah from the Quran that reminds you of the Hereafter.\nInvoke Allah with his Holy Names: (Most Forbearing) and (All-Forgiving) to treat you with His forbearance, forgive your sins and overlook your misdeeds.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil of heedlessness.\nguid\nThe worst and most hideous saying is that which slanders Allah's divine entity.\nThe lack of understanding the Quran may be a punishment for sins, so hasten to repentance, and ask often for Allah's forgiveness.\nRemembrance of Allah -especially the word of monotheism and recital of the Quran- is a cause for protecting the servant from the devils.\nrefl\nأَفَأَصۡفَىٰكُمۡ رَبُّكُم بِٱلۡبَنِينَ وَٱتَّخَذَ مِنَ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ إِنَٰثًاۚ إِنَّكُمۡ لَتَقُولُونَ قَوۡلًا عَظِيمٗا ٤٠\nAllah describes their claim as no more than a (say) since it was uttered without thinking because had the one who said that reflected on it slightly, he would have found it irrational. Ibn Ashur: 15/108.\nAllah describes the polytheists' claim that the angels are the daughters of Allah as a mere (say). Why?\nتُسَبِّحُ لَهُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ ٱلسَّبۡعُ وَٱلۡأَرۡضُ وَمَن فِيهِنَّۚ وَإِن مِّن شَيۡءٍ إِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمۡدِهِۦ وَلَٰكِن لَّا تَفۡقَهُونَ تَسۡبِيحَهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ حَلِيمًا غَفُورٗا ٤٤\nThe use of the statement, (you do not understand) and not, \"you do not know\", indicates that the mentioned knowledge is of a subtle nature. Ibn Ashur: 15/115.\nAllah says, (you do not understand) and not \"you do not know.\" Why?\nوَإِذَا قَرَأۡتَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ جَعَلۡنَا بَيۡنَكَ وَبَيۡنَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ حِجَابٗا مَّسۡتُورٗا ٤٥\nDescribing this veil as (concealed) indicates a high degree of obscurity so much so that the veil itself is concealed by another. Or, it means that this veil is different from all others because it is invisible. Ibn Ashur: 15/117.\nWhat is the benefit of describing the veil as (concealed) in this verse?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ أَكِنَّةً أَن يَفۡقَهُوهُ\nMeaning: Covers and lids so that they do not understand the meanings of the Quran; rather they listen to it in such a way that proof is established against them. Al-Saadi: 459.\nWhat indicates the existence of a cover or a lid on the heart?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ أَكِنَّةً أَن يَفۡقَهُوهُ وَفِيٓ ءَاذَانِهِمۡ وَقۡرٗاۚ\n(And deafness in their ears), Allah made those polytheists hard of hearing; hence, they did not hear the Quran which was recited before them, and this was a part of the concealed partition. The covers on their hearts and the deafness in their ears are a punishment from Allah to deprive them of the guidance of the Quran because of their evil intentions. Allah has not wronged them, but they wronged themselves by detesting the Messenger (ﷺ) and his Message, and fighting him and what he conveyed to them of true faith and the Oneness of Allah. Al-Jaza'iri: 3/199.\nWhat is the punishment, mentioned in this verse, for detesting what the Messenger (ﷺ) conveyed?\nوَإِذَا ذَكَرۡتَ رَبَّكَ فِي ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ وَحۡدَهُۥ وَلَّوۡاْ عَلَىٰٓ أَدۡبَٰرِهِمۡ نُفُورٗا ٤٦\nAbu Al-Jawza', Aws bin Abdullah said: There is nothing that drives away satan from the heart like saying, \"There is no deity but Allah\", then he recited: (And when you mention your Lord alone in the Quran, they turn their backs in aversion). Al-Qurtubi: 13/95.\nHow do you drive satan from your heart?\nنَّحۡنُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا يَسۡتَمِعُونَ بِهِۦٓ\nMeaning: We only kept them from benefiting when they hear the Quran because We know that their aim is wrong; they want to find the least reason to criticize it. They are not listening for the purpose of seeking guidance or accepting the truth; rather their intention is not to follow it. One who is like that will not benefit from listening to it in the slightest. Al-Saadi: 459.\nWhat is the best way to benefit from listening to the Quran?\nwords\nمَلُومًاBlamed by others and yourself\nمَدحُورًاBanished from Allah's mercy\nأَفَأَصفَاكُمHas He favored you?\nصَرَّفنَاWe have explained things in various ways\nأَكِنَّةًCovers\nوَقرًاDeafness\nوَرُفَاتًاCrumbled particles"],[287,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nSay good words to your brother or friend to increase cordiality between you and him.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the temptations of the devil.\nIn adherence to the command of the Messenger (ﷺ), write your will today.\nguid\nGet used to always saying good words.\nThe love of Allah, hope for His reward, and fear of His punishment are three deeds of the heart which are the origins of every good deed. That is why Allah attributes these deeds to those who are closer to Him.\nWhen corruption spreads out, the doom becomes near.\nrefl\nوَيَقُولُونَ مَتَىٰ هُوَۖ قُلۡ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَكُونَ قَرِيبٗا ٥١\nThere is no benefit in knowing the exact time of it; rather the benefit is to affirm it, establish it as a certain belief. Otherwise, everything that is coming is near at hand. Al-Saadi: 460.\nThe polytheists' question about the time of the Day of Resurrection is inappropriate. Why?\nيَوۡمَ يَدۡعُوكُمۡ فَتَسۡتَجِيبُونَ بِحَمۡدِهِۦ وَتَظُنُّونَ إِن لَّبِثۡتُمۡ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ٥٢\nIf a man lived for thousands of years in this worldly life and in his grave, he would consider that a very short time compared to the Day of Resurrection and eternity. Qatadah said: They will belittle the time span of this worldly life compared to the Day of Resurrection. Al-Baghawi: 2/687.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, why will man think that his dwelling in this worldly life was short?\nوَقُل لِّعِبَادِي يَقُولُواْ ٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُۚ\nIf there is a choice between two good things, then it is enjoined to give precedence to the better of the two when it is not possible to combine both. Speaking good words leads to developing good manners and doing righteous deeds, for the one who controls his tongue will be in control of all his affairs. Al-Saadi: 460.\nWhat is the difference between better and best? Which one we are enjoined of?\nوَقُل لِّعِبَادِي يَقُولُواْ ٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُۚ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ يَنزَغُ بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ\nThe devil strives to create trouble between people in a manner that is detrimental to their religious commitment and worldly affairs. The remedy for that is not to obey him, by avoiding the inappropriate talk to which he calls people, and by being soft and gentle with one another, so as to suppress the devil who seeks to spread discord among them, because he is their true enemy whom they should oppose. Al-Saadi: 460.\nThe devil gets in the conversation between you and others. How should you handle that?\nوَقُل لِّعِبَادِي يَقُولُواْ ٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُۚ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ يَنزَغُ بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ كَانَ لِلۡإِنسَٰنِ عَدُوّٗا مُّبِينٗا ٥٣\nThe important aim of this directive is to educate the Muslims to treat each other in kindness and with soft speaking because words reflect intentions. Moreover, it educates them on how to argue with the polytheists in order to avoid the consequences of quarrels and harshness, which can increase their hardheadedness and stubbornness, and that is satan's sowing discord between them and their enemy. Ibn Ashur: 15/132.\nWhat is the important aim of this verse?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ يَبۡتَغُونَ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمُ ٱلۡوَسِيلَةَ أَيُّهُمۡ أَقۡرَبُ وَيَرۡجُونَ رَحۡمَتَهُۥ وَيَخَافُونَ عَذَابَهُۥٓۚ\nWorship cannot be complete or perfect unless it is accompanied by both fear and hope. Fear stops one from doing things that are forbidden, and hope makes him do more good deeds. Ibn Kathir: 3/46.\nFor the believer, why is it important to have both fear and hope?\nوَإِن مِّن قَرۡيَةٍ إِلَّا نَحۡنُ مُهۡلِكُوهَا قَبۡلَ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ أَوۡ مُعَذِّبُوهَا عَذَابٗا شَدِيدٗاۚ كَانَ ذَٰلِكَ فِي ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مَسۡطُورٗا ٥٨\nIbn Masoud (t) said: \"When fornication and usury spread in a town, Allah decrees its destruction.\" Al-Qurtubi: 13/107.\nWhen does Allah decree the destruction of towns?\nwords\nفَسَيُنغِضُونَThey will nod their heads in ridicule\nيَنزَغُHe sows discord\nيَبتَغُونَThey seek\nالوَسِيلَةَMeans of nearness through obedience\nالكِتَابِThe Preserved Tablet\nمَسطُورًاIt is inscribed"],[288,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nShare a message about the risk of singing and music being steps of the devil.\nEnsure that you say your Athkar today, the morning and evening Athkar, the Athkar before and after eating your food, and Athkar when entering and leaving the house.\nSupplicate Allah to make you among His servants over whom the devil has no power.\nguid\nEven though Allah encompasses all people, He is, indeed, the most Forbearing with their disobediences.\nWhoever does not adhere to the rules of Sharia with respect to his wealth, children and food, the devil becomes his partner in them.\nLook for the traits of those over whom the devil has no power, and strive to be one of them.\nrefl\nوَءَاتَيۡنَا ثَمُودَ ٱلنَّاقَةَ مُبۡصِرَةٗ فَظَلَمُواْ بِهَاۚ وَمَا نُرۡسِلُ بِٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ إِلَّا تَخۡوِيفٗا ٥٩\nThamud and its sign are mentioned because of their fame among Arabs, and their ruined homes are in close proximity of the people of Makkah who see them while traveling between Makkah and the Levant. Ibn Ashur: 15/144.\nThamud is singled out for mention in this verse, why?\nوَمَا جَعَلۡنَا ٱلرُّءۡيَا ٱلَّتِيٓ أَرَيۡنَٰكَ إِلَّا فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلنَّاسِ وَٱلشَّجَرَةَ ٱلۡمَلۡعُونَةَ فِي ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِۚ وَنُخَوِّفُهُمۡ فَمَا يَزِيدُهُمۡ إِلَّا طُغۡيَٰنٗا كَبِيرٗا ٦٠\nWhen the Prophet (ﷺ) told the Polytheists about the event of Isra' (night Journey to Jerusalem) and the tree of Zaqqum, some of them denied him and claimed that was inconceivable. Then, Allah revealed this verse, (And We did not make the sight which We showed you except as a test for people, as well as the cursed tree [mentioned] in the Quran), it was a trial for the people so that the believer would be distinguished from the disbeliever. Moreover, he told them that he saw Paradise and Hellfire of which he warned them. Allah said, (We threaten them, yet it only increases them to greater transgression). Ibn Taimyah: 4/235.\nThe sight that was shown to the Prophet (ﷺ) was a trial for people. How?\nوَنُخَوِّفُهُمۡ فَمَا يَزِيدُهُمۡ إِلَّا طُغۡيَٰنٗا كَبِيرٗا ٦٠\nThe verbs (threaten) and (increases) are in the present tense form to indicate recurrence and renewal of threatening, but with it, their transgression recurs and increases. Ibn Ashur: 15/149.\nIn this verse, the verbs (threaten) and (increases) are in the present tense. Why?\nقَالَ أَرَءَيۡتَكَ هَٰذَا ٱلَّذِي كَرَّمۡتَ عَلَيَّ لَئِنۡ أَخَّرۡتَنِ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ لَأَحۡتَنِكَنَّ ذُرِّيَّتَهُۥٓ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ٦٢\n(I will surely overpower his offspring), I will surely seize and lead them. In the Arabic text, the word used for (overpower) is derived from a term for animal bridle which makes it follow its keeper. Ibn Juzay: 1/491.\nThe devil bridles man, what does that mean? What is the sign of that?\nوَٱسۡتَفۡزِزۡ مَنِ ٱسۡتَطَعۡتَ مِنۡهُم بِصَوۡتِكَ\nThe devil's voice is everyone who invites to the disobedience of Allah, the Almighty. Ibn Abbas (t) and Mujahid said: \"The devil's voice is singing, blowing into flutes, and diversion.\" Al-Qurtubi: 13/118.\nHow does the devil entice people with his voice?\nوَٱسۡتَفۡزِزۡ مَنِ ٱسۡتَطَعۡتَ مِنۡهُم بِصَوۡتِكَ وَأَجۡلِبۡ عَلَيۡهِم بِخَيۡلِكَ وَرَجِلِكَ\nThe devil's voice includes everyone who speaks for the disobedience of Allah, everyone who blows into a flute, and everyone who beats a tambourine or a drum. The devil's soldiers include anyone who strives on his feet to disobey Allah. The devil's horse soldiers include every one who takes a ride to disobey Allah. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/142-143.\nExplain the meanings of the devil's voice, his horse soldiers, and foot soldiers.\nوَشَارِكۡهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰلِ وَٱلۡأَوۡلَٰدِ وَعِدۡهُمۡۚ وَمَا يَعِدُهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ إِلَّا غُرُورًا ٦٤\nBecoming a partner in their wealth is by earning it through usury, and spending it in disobedience. Becoming a partner in their children is begetting them through adultery, and by giving the child a name suggesting that he is a slave (abd) of something other than Allah, such as: Abd-Shams, Abd-Harith, and so on. Ibn Juzay: 1/492.\nGive examples of the devil's partnering in people's wealth and children.\nwords\nأَرَأَيتَكَTell me, do you see this one\nلأَحتَنِكَنَّI will surely overpower them\nمَوفُورًاAmple\nوَاستَفزِزEntice, and hasten\nوَأَجلِبMobilize and assault\nبِخَيلِكَ وَرَجِلِكَYour horses and foot soldiers"],[289,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nRecall a situation from which Allah saved you and thank Him for that.\nAsk Allah to have your record given to you in your right hand.\nEven the Prophet (ﷺ) needed help from Allah to stand firm, so, say, \"O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in all my affairs, and the determination in following the right path.\"\nguid\nAfter a servant is saved by Allah from adversary, he soon reverts to his heedlessness, evasion and corruption, which is an indication of his weakness.\nDo not disdain anyone for his skin color, lineage or country of origin.\nThe criminals will not accept you as a friend unless you join them in their sins.\nrefl\nأَفَأَمِنتُمۡ أَن يَخۡسِفَ بِكُمۡ جَانِبَ ٱلۡبَرِّ أَوۡ يُرۡسِلَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ حَاصِبٗا ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُواْ لَكُمۡ وَكِيلًا ٦٨\nThis verse points to the fact that safety on land is a great blessing from Allah that you often forget. If the land should swallow you up, you will be doomed with no chance for escape, which is in contrast to the adversity at sea. Ibn Ashur: 15/162.\nSafety on land is a great blessing that we often forget. How does this verse indicate that?\nوَفَضَّلۡنَٰهُمۡ عَلَىٰ كَثِيرٖ مِّمَّنۡ خَلَقۡنَا تَفۡضِيلٗا ٧٠\nThe reliable explanation for this preference is that it is based on the human ability to reason which is the basis of accountability. Moreover, through this ability, man knows about Allah, understands His Words, and believes in His reward and Messengers. Since this human ability alone is not sufficient to realize all that is required of man, Allah sent Messengers and revealed the Scriptures. The example of Sharia is like the Sun and the human mind is like the eyes, and so when they are open, they see clearly the Sun and realize the details of things. Al-Qurtubi: 13/126.\nExplain the reason that Allah prefers the children of Adam over much of what He created.\nيَوۡمَ نَدۡعُواْ كُلَّ أُنَاسِۢ بِإِمَٰمِهِمۡۖ فَمَنۡ أُوتِيَ كِتَٰبَهُۥ بِيَمِينِهِۦ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يَقۡرَءُونَ كِتَٰبَهُمۡ وَلَا يُظۡلَمُونَ فَتِيلٗا ٧١\nA thread is a strand which is found in the middle of a date seed. This means that their deeds will not be lessened by as much as thread let alone more than that. Ibn Juzay: 1/493.\nWhy is the word (thread) used In this verse?\nوَمَن كَانَ فِي هَٰذِهِۦٓ أَعۡمَىٰ فَهُوَ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ أَعۡمَىٰ وَأَضَلُّ سَبِيلٗا ٧٢\n(This) refers to the life of this world; (blind) is the blindness of the heart. This means that whoever is blind from the truth in this life, will be blind on the Day of Resurrection, that is bewildered and despairing. Ibn Juzay: 1/493.\nWhat is the meaning of blindness in this life and in the Hereafter?\nوَإِن كَادُواْ لَيَفۡتِنُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ لِتَفۡتَرِيَ عَلَيۡنَا غَيۡرَهُۥۖ وَإِذٗا لَّٱتَّخَذُوكَ خَلِيلٗا ٧٣\nMeaning: You [O Prophet] should understand that they only oppose you and show enmity to you because of the truth that you have brought, not because of your character. Al-Saadi: 464.\nWhat is the reason for the Polytheists' enmity toward the Prophet (ﷺ)? How does a preacher to Islam benefit from that?\nوَلَوۡلَآ أَن ثَبَّتۡنَٰكَ لَقَدۡ كِدتَّ تَرۡكَنُ إِلَيۡهِمۡ شَيۡـٔٗا قَلِيلًا ٧٤\nThese verses point to the individual's great need for Allah to make him steadfast, that he should keep beseeching his Lord, asking Him to make him firm in his faith, and he should continue striving by all means to attain that, because Allah said to the Prophet (ﷺ) who is the most perfect of all people: (Had We not made you stand firm, you would nearly have inclined to them a little), so how about others who are below him? Al-Saadi: 464.\nThese verses indicate the individual's great need for Allah to make him steadfast. Explain.\nإِذٗا لَّأَذَقۡنَٰكَ ضِعۡفَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ وَضِعۡفَ ٱلۡمَمَاتِ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُ لَكَ عَلَيۡنَا نَصِيرٗا ٧٥\nThe higher a person's status is and the more blessings he receives from Allah, the greater his sin and the more serious the offence will be if he does something blameworthy, because Allah reminded His Messenger (ﷺ) that if he did that - although he is far above doing such a thing- then: (We would have made you taste double punishment, both in this life and after death. Thereupon, you would have found no helper against Us). Al-Saadi: 464\nAn offence committed by the Prophet (ﷺ), a scholar or a preacher is considered more serious than when it is committed by others. Why?\nwords\nحَاصِبًاA storm of stones\nقَاصِفًا مِنَ الرِّيحِA violent storm that destroys everything\nبِإِمَامِهِمTheir leader whom they followed\nكَادُواThey were about\nلَيَفتِنُونَكَTo tempt you away"]])